      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bird-in-Hand%2C_Pennsylvania",
      "category": "etymology",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "In 1815 Daniel Gibbons built a brick house that became the foremost Underground Railroad station, aiding over 1,000 slaves to freedom.",
